<title>POLAND: Polish net reserves fall to $21.55 bln in Jan 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish net reserves fall to $21.55 bln in Jan 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency reserves, those held in the whole banking system, fell by $261 million in January 1-10 to $21.55 billion, the National Bank of Poland said.  </p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dollars)JAN 10	DEC 96  NOV 96</p>
<p>    Official reserves		N.A.	  N.A.   17.85</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.55	 21.81  21.46</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
